{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $11$ different letters in the word DOCUMENTARY, so $n=11.$ We want to select $3$ of those letters to make-up a $3$-letter word, so we have $r=3.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different made-up words is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{11}{P}_{3} & =\\frac{11!}{(11-3)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{11!}{8!} \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9\\cdot \\cancel{8!}}{\\cancel{8!}} \\\\  & =11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =990.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247858 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247859 13194139533709 true] [17592186247858 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247860 13194139533709 true] [17592186247858 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247861 13194139533709 true] [17592186247858 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247862 13194139533709 true] [17592186247858 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247863 13194139533709 true] [17592186247858 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533709 true] [17592186247858 1041 "selection" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247858 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247860 13194139533709 true] [17592186247858 1110 #uuid "d9bd0049-0e17-526c-9218-631155904f29" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247859 1034 "7\\,920" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247859 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533709 true] [17592186247859 1111 #uuid "3fd5239c-f70f-59cb-81c7-b20a82cac077" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247860 1034 "990" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247860 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533709 true] [17592186247860 1111 #uuid "52d5b905-46c1-5365-8d39-3ec33bc29bb9" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247861 1034 "1\\,331" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247861 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533709 true] [17592186247861 1111 #uuid "6953f119-85f0-5bb0-b6ba-6c52bd4002ca" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247862 1034 "99" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247862 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533709 true] [17592186247862 1111 #uuid "9e92f199-063e-550b-ae17-7b812f745e62" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247863 1034 "90" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247863 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533709 true] [17592186247863 1111 #uuid "eb87b9f5-6598-58fc-bd15-48bd334c74ed" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247864 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247865 13194139533709 true] [17592186247864 1089 "q-84980" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247864 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533709 true] [17592186247864 1100 "How many made-up $3$-letter words can be made using only $5$ vowels, where each vowel cannot appear in the word more than once?" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247864 1113 #uuid "dd18f01f-3465-5ee5-ab1c-02f5b61ab820" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247864 1138 false 13194139533709 true] [17592186247864 1145 "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $5$ vowels, so $n=5.$ We want to select $3$ of those vowels to make-up a $3$-letter word, so we have $r=3.$ \n\nTherefore, the number of different made-up words is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{5}{P}_{3} & =\\frac{5!}{(5-3)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5!}{2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot \\cancel{2!}}{\\cancel{2!}} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247866 13194139533709 true] [17592186247865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247867 13194139533709 true] [17592186247865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247868 13194139533709 true] [17592186247865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247869 13194139533709 true] [17592186247865 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247870 13194139533709 true] [17592186247865 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533709 true] [17592186247865 1041 "selection" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247865 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247867 13194139533709 true] [17592186247865 1110 #uuid "2dd98a53-3108-5dda-843a-58439d9a414f" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247866 1034 "20" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247866 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533709 true] [17592186247866 1111 #uuid "0749f2c7-e18f-5293-9518-2026a0ad6794" 13194139533709 true] [17592186247867 1034 "60" 13194139533709 true] [